    // a handed callable writes a value of the Type wherever its walk meets it in a value the call stores anew in storage it writes, a
    // second fact beside what the Type hides above (Binding.Writes reads both): past an owning handle (rc, arc) in such storage a fresh
    // handle brings a new payload (uniqTUniqRcFnBad: `set: (uniq/(rc/T) during u, E)` may store a fresh rc/T holding the child, so *x,
    // storage of f's kept T, can keep it), and so past a nested handle, a Field, a Tuple element, an Array element, an object borrow's
    // payload, a raw layer stating no Origin, a generic owning handle and a requirement of a Contract premise; never past a borrow,
    // whose referent is no storage the call makes (uniqTUniqRefFnOk, ownRcBorrowOk, rvRcUniqOk), a shared layer before the handle
    // (ownThroughSharedOk, ownContractRefRcOk), a handle the writer takes by value (ownByValueOk), a payload of another Type
    // (ownOtherPayloadOk) or a raw layer stating a borrow's Origin, which addresses only storage that Origin covers (rvRcRawOriginOk,
    // SPEC 5.7). Rows: the design's 17 (G935/own/labels.txt) and the reviewer's twins (C1-C3), labelled from SPEC before any output.
